    "id": "p-b640b5",
    "offset": 4037,
    "text": "[18] \"I merely mean to state that 2s. is the utmost weekly pension or allowance gratuitously given to a single able-bodied labourer. An applicant of this description, if he said that he could not live on his wages, would probably be taken into the poor-house, or set to work by the parish at perhaps 5s. a-week; but he would not receive for doing nothing more than 2s. a-week, while the sums which a married labourer receives for doing nothing increase with the birth of every additional child.\""
  },
